WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:05.270
From movies that deserve a second chance to
films that were so underrated that you might

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:09.300
not have even heard of them, we've rounded
up a selection of superhero films from the

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.020
past 15 years that don't receive much acclaim,
but may be worth a (re)watch.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:20.300
Hitting theaters less than two months after
Christopher Nolan's critically acclaimed Batman

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:25.920
Begins in 2005, Sky High offers a very different
take on superheroes than Nolan's gritty, grounded

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:26.420
saga.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:32.000
The movie follows Will Stronghold the son
of beloved superheroes the Commander and Jetstream

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:36.980
as he starts his classes at Sky High, a high
school in the clouds that's aimed at training

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:39.820
the children of supers to become the heroes
of the future.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:40.960
The only problem?

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:46.140
Will has no superpowers, which makes things
tricky when a villain takes all the super-parents

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:50.340
out of commission, and suddenly, it's on the
kids of Sky High to save the day.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:55.500
Although Sky High performed decently at the
box office and received generally positive

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.760
reviews, it was never truly able to establish
itself as a mainstay in the superhero canon.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:06.240
Perhaps after Batman Begins, viewers weren't
in the right mindset for a lighthearted, campy

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:10.820
romp, or perhaps adult audiences didn't fully
connect with the teen cast.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:16.080
Whatever the reason, Sky High didn't make
a huge splash when it came out, and it's mostly

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.100
faded from memory.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.700
However, don't let its modest performance
or poor staying power fool you.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:27.220
Sky High is an energetic, cheesy blast, filled
with heartwarming friendships, high-stakes

00:01:27.229 --> 00:01:32.040
adventure, and charmingly weird superpowers
from characters like the girl with the ability

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.820
to transform herself into a talking guinea
pig.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:35.600
"Magenta.

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:36.100
I shape-shift."

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:37.180
“Shape shift?”

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.480
“Into a Guinea pig.”

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:39.640
"Great."

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:45.580
Years before Nick Fury teased a project called
the "Avengers Initiative" and over a decade

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:51.280
before Deku started classes in My Hero Academia,
Sky High delivered a team of funny, endearing

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:53.680
superheroes the whole family could enjoy.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:59.659
If you've never heard of the 2006 superhero-themed
dramedy Special, you don't need to turn in

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:01.720
your superhero cred card just yet.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:06.700
Barely anyone saw the low-budget film during
its limited theatrical release.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:12.099
As for the plot, Special follows a man named
Les, played by Michael Rapaport, who believes

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:17.380
he's developed superpowers after experiencing
an adverse reaction during a clinical drug

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:17.880
trial.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:23.240
Despite attempts from his doctor and friends
to persuade him to stop taking the drug, Les

00:02:23.241 --> 00:02:27.760
becomes convinced that he was given these
powers for a reason, so he sets out to make

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:32.100
things better for the citizens of his town
by thwarting a series of small crimes.

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:37.959
However, as Les gains notoriety, the company
conducting the trial becomes increasingly

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:42.460
desperate to silence him, terrified that Les'
antics will cost them their funding.

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:47.740
While Special is a departure from standard
superhero tropes in that Les only thinks he

00:02:47.741 --> 00:02:52.910
has powers in reality, he's running into walls
when he believes he's phasing through them

00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:57.819
and flailing on the floor when he thinks he's
flying its themes couldn't be more true to

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:03.030
the genre, as Les wrestles with whether his
powers make him special, or if he can be special

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:03.520
without them.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.700
Even when the film feels a little uneven,
Rapaport's earnest performance, along with

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:12.180
the film's unique premise, makes Special truly
worthy of its title.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:18.040
Hancock follows an angry, irritable amnesiac
who proves that having superpowers doesn't

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.700
necessarily make you a hero.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:25.840
Finding himself hated by the public for his
surly disposition, John Hancock hires a public

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.400
relations specialist to rehabilitate his image.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:33.540
As a result, he winds up not only making a
few more enemies, but also discovering a piece

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:37.040
of information about his past that will change
his entire future.

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:42.940
Despite its solid premise and a valiant lead
effort by Will Smith, the 2008 film faltered

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:47.880
in the execution, alienating critics with
its uneven narrative and abrupt tonal shifts.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:53.080
What could have been a delightfully subversive
superhero story wound up being more convoluted

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:57.860
than surprising, with unearned twists that
strained the limits of the film's thin internal

00:03:57.860 --> 00:03:58.360
logic.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:04.200
Still, strong performances from Smith, Charlize
Theron, and Jason Bateman go a long way toward

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:09.200
rescuing Hancock from its own worst impulses,
and if you can go along with the bizarrely

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:14.100
contorted storytelling, there's a lot to appreciate
in the off-beat, quirky script.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:18.800
Smith checks his characteristic charm at the
door, fully embracing his off-putting character

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.380
and committing to every weird turn of the
plot.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:25.300
But instead of pushing the audience away,
he only draws us in more.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:29.400
Hancock is far from a perfect film, but it
still deserves some points for how hard it

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:29.900
tries.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:35.840
Between his short-lived tenure as the Human
Torch in The Fantastic Four and his definitive

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:41.660
performance as Captain America, MCU star Chris
Evans headlined yet another superhero action

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:44.980
thriller, although we don't blame anyone for
forgetting about this one.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:51.300
In 2009's Push, Evans plays Nick, a "mover"
who can use his telekinetic abilities to affect

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.480
the objects around him.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:56.599
Nick is far from the only superpowered person
in his world, though.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:05:01.740
He is joined by Cassie, played by Dakota Fanning,
a "watcher" who gets visions of the future

00:05:01.749 --> 00:05:07.020
and tells Nick they must find a way to save
his ex-girlfriend Kira from a variety of superpowered

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:10.340
enemies who will stop at nothing to get her
under their control.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:16.099
Of course, the convoluted plot of Push is
far, far more complicated than that, jammed

00:05:16.099 --> 00:05:21.539
so full of side characters, subplots, and
twists that it's easy to get lost in its winding,

00:05:21.539 --> 00:05:27.009
adrenaline-filled corridors Still, especially
for MCU fans, it's a lot of fun to see Evans

00:05:27.009 --> 00:05:31.479
embody a different character with the same
inherent likability and determination that

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:33.620
we're so used to seeing from Steve Rogers.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:37.460
Plus, his sibling-esque chemistry with Fanning
is delightful to watch.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:38.660
"It's not gonna happen okay?

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.180
“Tell me that I’m a crappy artist and
I’m wrong.”

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.680
“You are a crappy artist and you are wrong."

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:50.900
Sure, the story itself is more than a little
bizarre, and it works hard to set up a sequel

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:55.270
that in all likelihood will never happen,
but today's superhero fans are so used to

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:59.490
following intricate, sprawling storylines
that it shouldn't be a problem to sit back

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:00.580
and enjoy the ride.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:06.099
In the world of animated superhero films,
the past fifteen years have been, shall we

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:07.880
say ... incredible?

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:13.660
From The Incredibles to Big Hero 6 to Spider-Man:
Into the Spider-Verse, animated films have

00:06:13.669 --> 00:06:18.120
been the source of some of the most innovative
and creative superhero storytelling across

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:18.920
the genre.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:23.980
However, in the midst of this golden age of
animated superheroes, one super-film came

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:28.340
and went without much fanfare, despite its
largely positive reviews.

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:33.840
Megamind follows an alien supervillain voiced
by Will Ferrell who, after finally defeating

00:06:33.849 --> 00:06:39.439
the Superman-like hero Metro Man, realizes
his life lacks meaning and decides to create

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:40.560
a new hero to battle.

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:45.720
Unfortunately, Megamind's creation turns out
to be more villainous than he'd intended,

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:50.640
and in order to stop him, Megamind is ultimately
forced to step into the role of hero himself.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:55.619
It was bad luck for Megamind that another
animated supervillain-turned-reluctant-hero

00:06:55.619 --> 00:07:00.319
film had come out just a few months before
it hit theaters: Illumination Entertainment's

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:05.820
far more successful Despicable Me, which instantly
took the edge off Megamind's premise.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:11.500
Still, with a first-rate cast that also boasts
the vocal talents of Tina Fey and Jonah Hill,

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:16.520
Megamind is a visually impressive animated
adventure that, while never completely breaking

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:21.420
new ground, is still a fun spin on the reluctant
hero trope, and is probably better than you

00:07:21.480 --> 00:07:21.980
remember.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:26.800
Thor: The Dark World didn't get the worst
reviews when it first hit theaters, and it

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.940
was certainly profitable at the box office.

00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:33.540
However, when asked to rank the entries in
the Marvel CInematic Universe, The Dark World

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:36.840
tends to appear near the bottom of most Marvel
fans' lists.

00:07:37.669 --> 00:07:41.699
When you stack it up against high points like
Captain America: The Winter Soldier and Guardians

00:07:41.699 --> 00:07:46.989
of the Galaxy, The Dark World pales in comparison,
with a clunky script that turns one of Thor's

00:07:46.989 --> 00:07:51.180
greatest comic book foes into one of the MCU's
most forgettable villains.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:54.660
But The Dark World may have more going for
it than you recall.

00:07:54.920 --> 00:08:00.260
While the first Thor painted its hero as formal,
stiff, and pompous, The Dark World allowed

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:04.099
him to loosen up a little, hinting at the
sharp comedic turn the series would eventually

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:05.639
take in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:06.980
"I accept your surrender."

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:12.100
The Dark World also set up the post-Avengers
reconciliation between Thor and Loki, helping

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:16.319
build the relationship between the two brothers
into one of the strongest emotional arcs in

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:17.520
the entire MCU.

00:08:18.020 --> 00:08:22.419
Just try watching Thor and Loki team up to
steal a spaceship without cracking a smile,

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:23.000
we dare you.

00:08:23.820 --> 00:08:28.260
2009's Defendor received only a limited theatrical
release in the U.S.

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:32.840
It's a shame because Woody Harrelson gives
a stellar, heart-wrenching performance as

00:08:32.849 --> 00:08:37.519
Arthur Poppington, a man convinced that the
real world works just like the stories in

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:39.820
the comic books his grandfather taught him
to read.

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:45.640
Every night, Arthur dresses up as the superhero
Defendor and goes out in search of his arch-nemesis,

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.880
whom he blames for the death of his mother.

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:53.980
While it does play into a few of the superhero
genre's more tired tropes, Defendor is mostly

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:58.050
an entertaining, engaging film that's better
than its lack of commercial success would

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:58.720
suggest.

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:04.200
Harrelson's sincere portrayal of Arthur pairs
beautifully with Kat Dennings' trademark directness,

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:08.800
and Sandra Oh plays her scenes as Arthur's
court-ordered therapist with a deep warmth

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:11.670
and compassion that help balance the film's
darker moments.

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:17.500
Similar to The Dark World, Avengers: Age of
Ultron is the other black sheep in the Marvel

00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:18.000
family.

00:09:18.400 --> 00:09:22.580
This time, the reviews weren't all bad, but
the critics definitely took points for its

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:27.960
inconsistent characterization, disjointed
storytelling, and slapdash internal logic.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:33.740
But although Age of Ultron doesn't manage
to recreate the precise alchemy of The Avengers,

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:36.620
it still has a few big factors working in
its favor.

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:40.870
The party scene in which all of the Avengers
try to lift Thor's hammer feels straight out

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:44.910
of the comics, with every character getting
to relax and showcase their personalities

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:48.220
in a way the previous movies hadn't been able
to fully portray.

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:53.100
Fan-favorite characters the Vision and Scarlet
Witch, along with her brother, Quicksilver,

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:56.100
are introduced, and each get multiple moments
to shine.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:01.420
Ultron himself is actually one of Marvel's
better villains, brought to life with a deliciously

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:04.160
sinister vocal performance from James Spader.

00:10:04.680 --> 00:10:09.680
It even has some of the MCU's best action,
hands down, when the Hulk takes on Iron Man

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:10.180
in the second act.

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:16.240
"I'm sorry."

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:21.600
Viewed alongside the rest of the MCU, it's
understandable that Age of Ultron often finds

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:25.839
itself at the bottom of the heap, but even
though its flaws are both more numerous and

00:10:25.839 --> 00:10:29.779
more glaring than most of the films in its
company, that doesn't make it bad.

00:10:29.779 --> 00:10:34.350
And if we could all be a little forgiving,
then fans would see that Age of Ultron is

00:10:34.350 --> 00:10:36.399
actually a worthy entry in the MCU.

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:42.790
Based on the immensely hokey but highly beloved
'90s television series, the reimagined Power

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:47.850
Rangers brought together a group of just-before-they-hit
teen actors to play the diverse group of high

00:10:47.850 --> 00:10:52.639
school students who are granted superpowers
in order to protect the Earth from supervillain

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:53.540
Rita Repulsa.

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:59.280
Instead of jumping straight into the acrobatic
action that characterized the original series,

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:04.290
the film takes its time in allowing its characters
to master their powers, and in the process,

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:06.800
the Rangers develop a closer bond with one
another.

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:11.899
While critics were largely unimpressed, saying
the film failed to live up to both the television

00:11:11.899 --> 00:11:17.689
series and other contemporary superhero films,
Saban's Power Rangers still delivered many

00:11:17.689 --> 00:11:22.350
of the things that endeared fans to the original
series, such as the strong connections between

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:25.160
the characters, and of course, the Megazord.

00:11:25.709 --> 00:11:29.899
This version of Power Rangers may not focus
as much on fight scenes and one-liners as

00:11:29.899 --> 00:11:34.879
its predecessor, but it's still a lot of fun,
and its emphasis on character over spectacle

00:11:34.879 --> 00:11:39.399
may even feel preferable to some viewers who've
grown accustomed to the slow-burn development

00:11:39.399 --> 00:11:40.399
of the MCU.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:46.290
Based on the young adult novel by Alexandra
Bracken, The Darkest Minds takes place in

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:50.199
a world in which a mysterious virus has wiped
out the majority of the children and left

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.640
the few survivors with strange new powers.

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:57.300
In the United States, once the government
realizes what their children can do, they

00:11:57.301 --> 00:12:03.069
begin rounding all the kid up in camps, categorizing
them by ability and holding them indefinitely

00:12:03.069 --> 00:12:05.920
until the people in power can figure out what
to do with them.

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:11.040
The Darkest Minds follows a group of these
children, led by teen protagonist Ruby, as

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:15.569
they attempt to make sense of their abilities
and find a way to live in this dangerous new

00:12:15.569 --> 00:12:18.960
world, while also remaining hidden from the
adults who are tracking them.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:23.980
Sadly, The Darkest Minds received mostly negative
reviews from critics and bombed at the box

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:27.900
office, but it's worth noting that most of
its target audience seemed to like it.

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:32.480
For fans of dystopian teen adventures like
The Hunger Games, there's plenty to like about

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:36.850
The Darkest Minds, from its stirring themes
of empowerment and friendship to its endearing

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:37.960
ensemble cast.

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:43.180
And for superhero fans, the X-Men-like powers
exhibited by the kids everything from ripping

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:48.149
trees out of the ground, to shooting electricity
from their fingers, to altering a person's

00:12:48.149 --> 00:12:52.640
thoughts with a single touch should be more
than enough reason to check this one out.

